WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.940
"The painting of Ariandel..."

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.900
"Well, rotted scrap of it, that is."

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:10.840
"Go on"

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.120
"take it"

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.480
"touch it..."

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.980
This is Gael.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.220
Once he was a hollow slave

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.240
an undead warrior used as fodder in the bleakest of battles.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.400
Now he searches for a second Ashen one to enter the painting,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.000
For the tales tell of two Ashes who'll burn Ariandel away.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.840
"And then, the Ashes were two."

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.120
[Laughing Sinisterly]

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.300
His story will have its time in the light, but not right now

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:50.000
Subscribe, and look for these videos, so we can give each character the attention to detail they deserve.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.100
But by the end of this video, you'll have a good understanding of the entire painted world.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.140
And our place within it

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.660
"Rejoice my new friend"

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.260
"For this is a true haven of the forlorn.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.460
"The cold and gentle painted world of Ariandel"

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.440
"Quick, go along find one for yourself"

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.000
"A sweetly rotting bed to lie upon"

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.680
Ariandel, like the Painted world of Ariamis, has always been a place for forlorn souls.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.560
Almost all of the beings here have a story that belongs in the outside world

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:35.860
Something that they're keen to forget, and a story sad enough that it would cause them to get sucked into the painting

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:41.440
For example, these warriors are the followers of Farron and, they should look familiar.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.820
Their pointed steel helms mark them as a set of warriors from the undead legion of Farron

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:53.940
Farron and its watchers fell to ruin of course, but the followers survived, forlorn.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.540
With a home, fallen to ruin, and compatriots dead or corrupted by the abyss,

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.220
it's easy to understand how they were pulled into the painting.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:11.460
Also pulled into the painting were the Millwood knights, an order said to fight hand in hand with the earth itself.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.800
These are the fights that will drain you to your last remaining Estus.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.280
Till you're climbing that tower to take out the bowman making your life hell.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:28.820
Here, in this tower, you'll find the Captains Ashes, these sort of allow you to piece together the missing chunk of the Millwood Knights story.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:38.320
Long ago, when the Millwood Knights lost the forest they called home, they began a journey so long that even thoughts of their sworn enemy washed away,

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.960
replaced by a vision of a cold and brittle wood.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.460
We'll talk about their sworn enemy,

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.720
the loss of their forest, and how that led to their journey to the painting soon.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.240
It's one of the more tragic stories.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.180
Finally, you make it to the bridge, and to the Chapel of Ariandel.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.700
"Well,"

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.320
"You look to be Unkindled."

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.880
"No bell tolls,"

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.920
"and yet you've slipped into the painting."

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.120
"Oh, no matter."

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.100
"If you've lost your way,"

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.640
The words of Lady Friede will guide you."

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.060
"Now go on inside, show respect, and listen carefully."

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.460
This, is Sir Vilhelm,

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.580
a knight completely loyal to the Lady inside.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.400
"Welcome, to the painted world of Ariandel."

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.220
"I am Friede."

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.900
"I have long stood beside our blessed Father, and the rest of the Forlorn."

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.880
"But Forlorn, thou seemeth not..."

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:42.540
"Ashen One,"

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.420
"I know not the missteps that led thee to this Painted World."

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.120
"But thy duty is all,"

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.280
"and thy duty lieth elsewhere."

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.840
"Return for whence thou cam'st."

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.780
"I presume it visible to thee?"

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.240
"The bonfire here, in this room."

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.880
"A meek, and faded thing."

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.160
"But t'will guide thee, nonetheless."

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:14.380
"Ahh yes, there is a thing thou shouldst by rights possess."

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:21.220
"Ours is a chance encounter, to be sure, but perhaps it was meant to be."

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:28.540
"Let this be a remembrance of this cold world, a thing to help thee bear thy duty."

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:29.880
"Now,"

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.440
"Return for whence thou cam'st."

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.140
"Thou'st a place in that world,"

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.680
"and that alone, is cause to rejoice."

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:44.300
This ring is given to you, because this ring was never meant to grace Friede's hand.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.220
The painting, and it's frost as well,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.080
it became her home.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.340
"Lady Friede has spoken, has she not?"

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.300
"Then tarry no longer, and begone."

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.520
"There is one thing you should know,"

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.660
"inside the cold painting,"

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.540
"curiosity could be your cross."

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.480
"Stray from the withering flame,"

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.880
"and the snow will swallow you whole."

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.740
(screeching)

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.860
Within the snow, are the crawling, crow like Corvians.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.960
And these Corvians are markedly different than the Corvians we've seen before,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.600
these ones are pitiful,

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.020
they're dragging their defilement along with them,

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.360
and they're barely even a threat.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.520
I think that this easy gameplay sequence is meant to reinforce that.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.420
Further along, we meet the creature that likely crippled them.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.240
This is a Corvian too, but it's a Corvian Knight.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:52.240
Does it look familiar? It has the same body structure and this same peck move as the crows of Velka did, in Dark Souls 1,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.680
and it's vicious.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:02.780
When we find the Corvian Knight weapons upon the rooftops, they reveal that the Corvian Knights became infatuated with Sister Friede,

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.920
the woman we met in the Ariandel Chapel just now.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:12.300
Like her, these creatures embraced the rot, and swore to protect the painting from fire,

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.540
this decision was what led them to execute their own brethren.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:22.700
And their brethren clearly had other ideas about fire and rot.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:30.100
"Hmm, well, there is nothing Forlorn about you."

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.680
"You must be the other Ash, I suppose?"

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.460
"Ohh, ohh, finally, you've come.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.920
"Oh wondrous Ash,"

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.380
"grant us our wish."

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.440
"Make the tales true,"

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.180
"and burn this world away."

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:59.700
"Surely you've seen the rot that afflicts our world."

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.340
"But that witch fooled the good father;"

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.600
"and buried the flame."

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.380
"After we had all made up our minds, too..."

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.040
"So,"

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.300
"please,"

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.000
"grant us one wish."

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.060
"My lady must see flame,"

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.740
"and you, only to show her."

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.440
"Oh, please,"

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.260
"it must be you."

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:34.680
"I'm so terribly frightened, of timidly rotting away..."

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.220
"Like those..."

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.260
"Like those fools on the outside."

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:46.660
This dialogue reveals a lot, and the story really starts to take shape here.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:50.160
This is a tale of fire versus rot,

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:55.900
and the Corvian at the start, with the feathers, he told us to embrace the rot,

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.040
and accept it.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:03.300
But Gael told us, this world needs a proper flame, that will burn the rost away

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:09.180
This creature tolls us once, that they all made up their minds to burn the world away,

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:10.620
rot, and all.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:16.200
Unfortunately, Friede came along, and convinced the Father otherwise.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:22.980
The Corvian Knights, infatuated with Friede, betrayed their brethren and enforced her rule.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:28.720
Friede asked us to leave this place, and Vilhelm threatened us to.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:36.700
They fear the second Ash, because, according to the tales, it is the second Ash that heralds the flame.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:43.640
So, it's our job to find the rest of the secrets in the painting, and, they're very close by.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.940
I've seen your kind,

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.500
time and time again.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.120
Every fleeing man must be caught.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.420
Every secret must be unearthed

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.060
Such is the conceit of the self proclaimed seeker of truth.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.320
But in the end, you lack the stomach.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.740
For the agony that you'll bring upon yourself...

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:11.920
From his items, we learn who Vilhelm, The Knight of Londor, really is.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.320
So he served the three sisters who founded the Sable Church,

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:21.040
and before this video, we only knew about two of these sisters.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:25.520
We talked a lot about them in the Hollows of Londor video, go and check that out.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:31.360
So there was Liliane, the youngest, who first spoke about a lot of their miracles.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:37.700
There was Yuria, the second-eldest, who guides us to become a Lord of Hollows in the base game,

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:43.400
and now we know the identity of the third sister, the eldest,  Elfriede.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.460
Vilhelm, his armor reads, was particularly loyal to the eldest.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.240
"Forgive me, my Lady."

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:56.220
"I swore an oath, but I have failed you."

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:00.140
"...Lady Elfriede..."

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:04.740
The contraption key leads to the attic of the archive.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:09.220
Long ago, Sir Vilhelm lead a white haired woman up here,

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.520
and kept this key, as it were his life.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.160
"I believe..."

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.000
"I feel the scent of Ash upon thee.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:22.000
"Thou'rt the one of whom Uncle Gael spoke."

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.680
"The one to show me the flame."

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.280
"Tis good."

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.480
"When this is done, may I return."

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.200
"The door is open thanks to thee."

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:36.980
"I'll head off to paint."

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:40.120
"I promised Uncle Gael I would."

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.760
I wonder what she's doing here,

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:48.640
and it's almost like she's scraping a dent in the table, out of some compulsion to paint, maybe?

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:52.100
We'll hear more from the white haried girl later.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.860
Did you notice this?

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:59.480
Entrenched in the snow is a bell that looks really similar to the one in Firelink,

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:02.180
albeit, with slightly different engravings.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:09.920
Our Firelink bell in Dark Souls III is what unearths the Unkindled from their graves, so that they can link the fire.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.980
And, think about this,

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:15.220
in a way, this world craves fire too.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:19.080
just like the world outside, and this world has a bell as well.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:24.360
The tales tell of a second Ash that will come and bring fire to the painting.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.040
Considering Vilhelm and Friede don't want fire,

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:31.420
it's logical, they wouldn't want no bell ringing either.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:36.820
And this explains why Vilhelm is surprised you made it here, even though there is no bell.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.220
"No bell tolls, and yet you've slipped into the painting."

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:45.360
Curious right? So I think thats why the bell is entrenched.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:50.680
And past Vilhem, below Elfriede, in the heart of the mountain

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:54.720
is this huge concentration of rot inflicting the world.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:12:00.260
Hidden, amongst the flies is the only way to unlock the vault behind Friede.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:06.920
A lever that looks, and functions, identically to the one in the Painted World of Dark Souls 1,

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:13.380
rotates a statue of a woman holding a young child, and, it opens the way.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:19.900
"As ashes will be, ever seeking fire."

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:26.940
"I see flame, flame flickering once again."

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.700
"Not enough blood yet shed."

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.720
"My flail.... Bring me my flail."

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:44.840
"Ahh, Friede. What stops thine ears?"

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:51.620
"Please, my flail, right away."

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:09.940
"Ahh, oh, bring Friede to me please."

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:18.120
"Can'st thou not see? The flame, flickering once again."

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:25.940
"Soon will it surge, I can see it, feel it..."

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:38.160
(ominous wind howling)

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:43.260
"Fret not father, we have no need of thy flail."

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:50.000
"Tis only the flame, quivering at misguided Ash."

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.260
"Please, avert thine eyes."

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:05.580
"I will snuff out these ashes for good."

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:14.020
This is a damn good boss fight, and for most of us I think it's going to help justify how short this DLC was.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:17.760
This first phase is tough, mainly because of this trick.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:27.140
All of the sudden, you're straining your ears for footsteps, knowing that this woman is  running towards you,

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.820
and not one hundred percent sure where it's going to come from.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.620
But once you get over your fear of this move, it actually becomes her weakness.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:37.180
You get the timing down, you figure out where she tends to move to

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.300
in her invisibility, and then, the match swings in your favor.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.140
Friede was the first Ash to enter the painting,

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:49.680
but together, with the Good Father, they chose rot over fire.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.280
When she disappears most of us said "Holy shit, just like Priscilla", right?

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.480
She certainly is taking after her.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:00.720
I've mentioned that Elfriede was a sister of the Sable Church,

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:06.300
but what I haven't really mentioned is that she renounced her former life, and,

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.160
discovered a people she wished to protect in the painting,

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.400
assuming the precise form that they yearned for.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:18.860
So she became this polite, scythe wielding Lady of the Painting.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:25.600
But, Elfriede isn't a half dragon crossbreed, like Priscilla was, she's Unkindled Ash,

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.960
and as such, she's supposed to seek flame.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:32.740
But instead, her and the father chose rot over fire.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:37.780
In order to suppress the flame, the father shreds his own skin,

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.520
that's why he asks for his flail at the start of the fight.

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:45.840
It's his blood that appeases the flame for, I quote:

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:51.200
"The painting was painted with blood, and only blood can protect the sacred."

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.620
And regardless of weather Elfriede manipulated the father into doing this,

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:02.060
he's completely dependent on her now, and you take her away from him.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:35.180
(unintelligible screaming)

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:39.920
(chains braking)

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.520
(unintelligible screaming)

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:57.880
(explosion)

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:40.100
(screams)

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.360
Ahhh.

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:05.540
Father, not Lloyd, disturbs the flame, and the flame brings Elfriede back,

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:11.280
which isn't too strange, considering the fire brings us back to life as well, as an Unkindled.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:16.680
And so, the two Ashes fighting causes the fire to flare.

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.460
The white haired woman is going to see flame.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:24.440
By enraging Ariandel, we're getting what we want, in a way.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.440
I need a break though, at this point, phase two is tough.

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:35.000
Upstairs now, in the chapel, she's moved, the white haired woman has returned to her canvas

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:38.860
and she wishes to paint a new world to replace this one.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.180
"Thou art Ash."

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:44.640
"Thou'st a pact made with Uncle Gael."

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.000
"So I wish to tell thee all."

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.040
"Behold its size."

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.680
"This is my canvas."

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:58.160
"It's to be a cold, dark and very gentle place."

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:03.120
"...But first, I must see flame."

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:10.080
"One day, it will make someone a goodly home. That's why I must see flame."

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:17.180
From this, we learn that new paintings can arise, when the old ones fall to rot.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:22.400
There was rot, in the old painting of Ariamis, also, don't forget

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.680
there was the poison spewing dragon, there was the Undead Phalanx,

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.720
there was the bloated monstrosities.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:34.280
In an unchanging canvas, which is home to the terrible, the unwanted, and the rotten,

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:39.120
maybe it makes a lot of sense for the rot to inevitably take over the painting.

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.580
So the painting of Ariamis undoubtedly fell,

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:47.220
but Father Ariandel is said to have restored the painting.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.700
This is his world he created,

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:55.320
and Friede came and convinced him not  to ever let go of his painting,

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:58.680
and so the rot took over, but they embraced it.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:03.140
Yet, a new creator lies waiting to paint a new vision.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:08.440
"Those who aren't ken to fire cannot paint a world."

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:14.620
"Those absorbed by fire, must not paint a world."

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.020
"Don't worry, I haven't forgotten Mother."

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:28.280
So with the white haired girl in mind, we kill Ariandel and Sister Friede once more.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:38.740
"Whe the Ashes are two, the flame alighteth."

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:44.800
"Thou'rt ash, and fire befits thee, of course..."

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:50.040
This little event here, is worthy of an entire video, pretty much.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:54.280
And you'll get one, but for now; what is Black Flame?

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.020
Well it's indicative of the Abyss that lies within man,

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:02.080
described as the impenetrable fires of humanity.

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:04.200
We'll leave it at that, for now.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:09.600
So for those of you who did this spoiler free, how incredible is this moment?

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:14.980
A three phase boss fight, where you empty a full health bar  each time.

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:18.800
It's unheard of and completely demoralizing.

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:22.480
Especially when you discover how  tough phase three is.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.720
It's like fighting Lady Maria of Bloodborne,

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:30.140
but with the slower character pacing of the Dark Souls series.

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:33.120
The best way I found to beat her,  my first time,

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:39.600
was to try and keep Gael alive in round two so that we could stun lock her together in round three.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:43.000
And when Gaels AI decided to behave,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:48.180
I got her low enough that I could take her out with my relatively under powered character.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:49.880
And that, is the end.

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:56.840
When we finish, we come face to face with a human with a snake for a lower body.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:00.900
This DLC has a lot of curiosities, and,

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.920
I hope you make this channel your place to explore them.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:10.260
But there's no curiosity more curious than this piece of dialogue that we receive at the end.

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:11.960
Thank you for watching.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.060
"My thanks, Ashen One."

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:18.280
"I can almost see the flame."

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:22.740
"Soon Uncle Gael will bring me the pigment."

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:25.680
"I wonder if he has found it?"

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.080
"The dark soul of man..."

